<title>USA: Life Re unit to acquire New American.</title>
<headline>Life Re unit to acquire New American.</headline>
<dateline>STAMFORD, Conn.</dateline>
<text>
<p>Life Re Corp. said Monday its wholly owned subsidiary, Reassure America Life Insurance Co., will acquire New American Life Insurance Co. for about $21 million.</p>
<p>The deal is subject to approval by insurance regulators.</p>
<p>New American is a privately held insurer based in Columbia, Mo.</p>
<p>Stamford, Conn.-based Life Re is a leading provider of life and health reinsurance. Its stock rose 25 cents to $34.875 on the New York Stock Exchange in morning trading.</p>
